<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n32206" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">octōgēnārĭus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj.
		octogeni, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>containing eighty</i> (post-Aug.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">exheredata ab octogenario patre,</span>”
				<i>who was a man of eighty</i>, <i>was eighty years
						old</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					Ep. 6, 33, 2</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Vulg. 2 Reg. 19, 35</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fistula,</span>”
				<i>eighty inches broad</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Vitr. 8,
					7</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">octōgē-nārĭus</span></b> ,
				ĭi, m., <i>a
				commander of eighty soldiers</i>, <i><span class="en">Inscr.
				Orell. 3628</span></i>.</div>
